k your wrist  outwards letting it roll off the tip of  your finger let's try it just like that  so this one's working pretty well now  again make sure that these are not bent  too much if you bend them too much this  is what will happen it will not fly very  fast because it's blocking too much air  it's not getting a lot of it's getting  too much air resistance so you see how  slow it goes so once again if you bent  them too much like this just set it down  on the table and just flatten it out  like that make sure you're holding it  properly put your pointer on top here  hold it like this angle it ever so  slightly and flick your wrist out flick  your wrist and let it roll off your  finger  [Music]  and there you go there is your cardboard  boomerang thank you guys so much for  watching my tutorial for the cardboard  tri-blade boomerang I hope you did enjoy  it and found it easy to follow  especially since I put a lot of work  into it with all the diagrams and  everything and I think it's a really  cool way to use excess cardboard that  you might have otherwise thrown away  I've been posting some stuff on my  Instagram and also my Rob's phone  channel so if you haven't checked those  channels out I'll definitely put some  links down below to my other social  media sites that you can check out that  I've been using a couple of people have  asked me about cubing and I actually  recently got some new cubes  I got again 3x3 and 4x4 magnetic and  also MOU 5x5 all of which have become my  favorite new cubes and I recently got a  sub 5 for all three of them which is  pretty that's really good for me  considering I've only been practicing  for a few weeks again please give the  video a thumbs up if you enjoyed it and  let me know what you'd like to see next  down in the comments below I do have  some other ideas that I've been writing  down some other origami stuff and some  non-related origami things that I've  been thinking about teaching but I just  wasn't sure people would actually want  to see it so you know maybe I'll do that  so I might put a pole up and see if you  guys want to see some of the things that  I am thinking about so I'll definitely  do my best to post more even if it's  just an update or cube solving video or  whatever it is something that I've been  wanting to teach so definitely be on the  lookout and I'll see you that

